      "/usr/share/sounds/scheme": {
        "content": "# Event-sound scheme (todos/0094), consulted by PlaySound/MessageBeep\n# (os/win32) and the wm startup chime through os/sounds.h. Three layers\n# overlaid per key, highest wins: ~/.config/sounds, /etc/sounds,\n# /usr/share/sounds/scheme. Lines: EVENT<ws>WAV-PATH; the value `none`\n# silences that event; the reserved key `mute on` silences all of them\n# (the Control Panel Sounds applet toggles it).\nSystemStart\t/usr/share/sounds/startup.wav\nSystemDefault\t/usr/share/sounds/ding.wav\nSystemHand\t/usr/share/sounds/chord.wav\nSystemQuestion\t/usr/share/sounds/ding.wav\nSystemExclamation\t/usr/share/sounds/chimes.wav\nSystemAsterisk\t/usr/share/sounds/ding.wav\nBell\t/usr/share/sounds/ding.wav\n"
      },
      "/usr/share/keys": {
        "content": "# Keyboard scheme (todos/0149), consulted by user32 (EDIT/LISTBOX verbs +\n# accelerators), term (copy/paste chord), the wm desktop and the Control\n# Panel Keyboard applet through os/keys.h. Three layers overlaid per key,\n# highest wins: ~/.config/keys, /etc/keys, /usr/share/keys. Keys:\n# scheme (windows | macos \u2014 which keymap; windows = Ctrl verbs, macos =\n# Cmd verbs + the emacs Ctrl rows in GUI text fields), readline (on |\n# off \u2014 those emacs rows; only meaningful under the macos scheme).\nscheme\twindows\nreadline\ton\n"
      },
      "/usr/share/display": {
        "content": "# Display configuration (hires-display), consulted by the Control Panel\n# Display applet (os/display.h) and the kernel worker's display-config\n# bridge to the page (os/kernel-worker.js). Three layers overlaid per key,\n# highest wins: ~/.config/display, /etc/display, /usr/share/display. Keys:\n# zoom (auto | 0.5 | 0.75 | 1 | 2 | 3 — the VT2 desktop zoom factor; >1\n# magnifies, <1 is high-density (more fits), auto = viewport default:\n# phone-shaped boots 2x, everything else 1x).\n# NB deliberately no baked `zoom` line: an ABSENT key is the automatic\n# default AND lets the page honor a pre-bridge localStorage choice; an\n# explicit user-layer `zoom auto` (the applet's Automatic) overrides that.\n"
      },
      "/usr/share/screensaver": {
        "content": "# Screensaver configuration (todos/0096), consulted by /bin/wm (the idle\n# raise) and the Control Panel Screen Saver applet through os/saver.h.\n# Three layers overlaid per key, highest wins: ~/.config/screensaver,\n# /etc/screensaver, /usr/share/screensaver. Keys: saver (none | marquee |\n# starfield), timeout (idle seconds; 0 disables), text (marquee banner).\nsaver\tstarfield\ntimeout\t900\ntext\tgucOS\n"
      },
      "/usr/share/term": {
        "content": "# Terminal configuration (todos/0273d), consulted by /bin/term (loaded at\n# startup, applied live, live-reloaded on a ~/.config watch) and edited by\n# its Shell > Settings... window. Three layers overlaid per key, highest\n# wins: ~/.config/term, /etc/term, /usr/share/term. Keys: fontsize (grid\n# font px, 8..32), theme (dark | light | green | amber | ocean), scrollback\n# (history lines, 0..10000; 0 disables), cursor (block | under | bar),\n# bell (sound | visual | none).\nfontsize\t14\ntheme\tdark\nscrollback\t2000\ncursor\tblock\nbell\tsound\n"
      },
      "/usr/share/sounds/startup.wav": {
        "bin": "os/sounds/startup.wav"
      },
      "/usr/share/sounds/ding.wav": {
        "bin": "os/sounds/ding.wav"
